 "No basta con saber cuánta gente descarga una app: importa cuánta vuelve.": "Knowing how many people download an app isn't enough: what matters is how many come back.",
 "Sin cohortes, los promedios mezclan usuarios nuevos y antiguos y engañan.": "Without cohorts, averages mix new and old users and mislead.",
 "Qué es una cohorte": "What a cohort is",
 "<b style=\"font-size:26px;color:#7048e8\">Un grupo con algo en común</b><br><span style=\"font-size:21px;color:#241a45\">Quienes se registraron la misma semana.</span>": "<b style=\"font-size:26px;color:#7048e8\">A group with something in common</b><br><span style=\"font-size:21px;color:#241a45\">Those who signed up the same week.</span>",
 "<b style=\"font-size:26px;color:#b0752c\">Se compara con otros grupos</b><br><span style=\"font-size:21px;color:#241a45\">Para ver si el producto mejora.</span>": "<b style=\"font-size:26px;color:#b0752c\">It's compared with other groups</b><br><span style=\"font-size:21px;color:#241a45\">To see whether the product is improving.</span>",
 "<b style=\"font-size:26px;color:#269790\">Se sigue en el tiempo</b><br><span style=\"font-size:21px;color:#241a45\">Cuántos vuelven al día 1, 7 y 30.</span>": "<b style=\"font-size:26px;color:#269790\">It's followed over time</b><br><span style=\"font-size:21px;color:#241a45\">How many come back on day 1, 7, and 30.</span>",
 "Pregunta qué parte de la curva es más importante cuidar. Casi todos dirán el primer día.": "Ask which part of the curve is most important to look after. Almost everyone will say the first day.",
